// Money, coins: a stack of a coin unit, kept in a household's coffer, and
// what goods are worth in them (VILLAGE.md decision 9, slice 9).
//
// Cut points:
// - full:     coins are a stack, counted when handed over (a split), merged
//             where they are put with others: a stall's takings, a coffer.
//             What a unit of goods is worth in coins to an agent is its
//             #Pricing: the most of those whose `valued` it believes the
//             goods to be, raised by what it feels of the need they serve.
//             What a seller asks moves with its stock: more when it has
//             little to spare, less when it has plenty.
// - reduced:  the same.
// - abstract: as reduced. Money as a coarse stock is planned
//             (DETAIL_REGIMES.md).
// - frozen:   the same: coins are things.
// - market:   a seller posts its pricing, by its stock; a buyer buys at a
//             posted price no more than its own (market/).
// - code:     agency_pricing (src/agency_agency.odin): a seller's stock is
//             what it believes is in the supply its stall is kept from, in
//             hand, or in a pack it carries. The tempting purse's money is
//             still cloth (money.tri).

package money

// A coin, a unit of a stack; a household starts with four hundred in its
// coffer (a coin is small money: a portion of grain is four).
#Coins:    #Stack & {}
coin:      #Coins & { material: "brass", unit: "coin", unitMass: 10g, count: 1 }
coins_400: #Coins & { material: "brass", unit: "coin", unitMass: 10g, count: 400 }

// Where a household keeps its coins.
coffer: #Container & { material: "oak", mass: 8kg, capacity: 4 }

coin_look:   #Look & { kindOf: "#Coins", look: "coins", prevails: 1 } @family(looks)
coffer_look: #Look & { kindOf: "coffer", look: "container.coffer" } @family(looks)

// What a unit of something like `valued` is worth to an agent in coins: its
// `coins`, the most of those whose `valued` it believes the thing to be;
// raised by what it feels of the need the thing serves (`pressure`), `per`
// tenths of a coin a point. With none, nothing: it isn't for sale, nor
// bought.
// What a seller asks for its spare goods goes by its stock of them: at
// `plenty` it asks `coins`; `asks` is a curve over its stock as a percent
// of `plenty` (agency.tri's #Point): what it asks, as a percent of
// `coins`. Never less than a coin.
#Pricing: #Need & { valued: #Body, coins: int & >=0 & <=1000, plenty: mass, asks: [...#Point] }

// Twice the price with nothing to spare, the price at plenty, half at four
// times that.
let by_stock = [{ input: 0, output: 200 }, { input: 100, output: 100 }, { input: 400, output: 50 }]

// Plenty: a household's grain for a month (fifty kilograms, two hundred
// portions); twenty kilograms of venison, a fortnight's meat; a tonne of
// firewood, a household's for a season.
grain_price:    #Pricing & { valued: #Stack & { unit: "grain" }, coins: 4, pressure: "hunger", per: 4, plenty: 50kg, asks: by_stock } @family(prices)
turnip_price:   #Pricing & { valued: #Stack & { unit: "turnip" }, coins: 4, pressure: "hunger", per: 4, plenty: 50kg, asks: by_stock } @family(prices)
venison_price:  #Pricing & { valued: #Stack & { unit: "venison" }, coins: 8, pressure: "hunger", per: 4, plenty: 20kg, asks: by_stock } @family(prices)
firewood_price: #Pricing & { valued: #Stack & { unit: "firewood" }, coins: 4, pressure: "cold", per: 4, plenty: 1000kg, asks: by_stock } @family(prices)
